SNA COLLECT Version 1.0  READ.ME file
-------------------------------------

Welcome to my Collection Manager

The archive should contain the following files:

\APP\SNACOLL0.APP                Main program.

\APP\SNACOLL\SNACOLLH.OVL        Optional Help file.
\APP\SNACOLL\SNACOLLP.OVL        Optional Print file.

\OPD\SNAPRINT.DYL        Optional Print file.  

README.NEW          'Get you started' instructions for new users (This file).

REGISTER.TXT        Details on how to register the program.
LICENCE.TXT         A legal licence.

HISTORY.TXT         Details of the various upgrades the program has gone through.

SNACOLL2.DOC        Full instructions in Word for Windows format.
SNACOLL2.TXT        Initial instructions in ASCII Text format.

DATA.ZIP            An example set of data files.

This is a fairly complex program, so I would strongly encourage you to 
read the instructions and work through the tutorial.  In particular, read the IMPORTANT
note in this file before you start to put in any data.

However, if you still insist on flying blind:

     1.   Put SNACOLL0.APP in your \APP\ directory

     2.   If you want to use the optional On-Line Help (Highly recommended)
          put the file SNACOLLH.OVL into an \APP\SNACOLL\ directory.

     3.   If you want to use the optional Print option put the file 
          SNACOLLP.OVL into the \APP\SNACOLL\ directory and the file
          SNAPRINT.DYL into an \OPD\ directory.  Note that this file is
          common to all my programs, so if you have more than one of
          them you only need one copy of this file.

     4.   Install (PSION-I) and go for it !!


IMPORTANT NOTE
--------------
Before you enter any data you really need to decide what you will want the program to 
accomplish.  In particular you need to decide what will be grouped in the 'Names' fields 
and what will go into the 'Categories' fields.  The difference to remember is that the 
filter function will operate on the 'Categories' and the Text search will work on the 
'Names' fields.   The other aspect to consider is the 'Sorting'.  If you sort on 
Category the order of the categories will be the order in which they were entered using
the 'Enter Category' option, so make sure you enter them in the order you want. 

If you do get a problem, PLEASE read the full instructions first.  

All comments, and registrations, gratefully received.

